WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:05.834
You guys look great.
Not only is this your first time

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.667
here, thank you for being here,
but for all of you,

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:10.234
this is your very first
late night talk show ever.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:12.467
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.901
-I'm honored.

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:18.434
The show "Reservation Dogs" has
gotten amazing accolades.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:21.467
It's over 80 critics'
best-of-TV lists.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.601
You won a Peabody Award.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:25.534
You won a Gotham Award
for Breakthrough Series.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:27.667
It's 98% on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:31.167
That's all great stuff.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.767
I want to get into the show.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.300
But I want to get to know a
little bit more about you guys.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.267
D'Pharaoh, talk to me.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:38.734
Were you always into acting?

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:42.133
Was that your plan?

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:44.367
-Um, not really.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.501
I mean, when I was a little kid,
we used to --

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:49.267
me and my twin brother used to
make little skits here and there

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:51.000
but I never thought I could
actually do it

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.734
or be on a stage like here.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.100
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.801
-And how did you hear
about the audition?

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:58.367
-Just like any other audition.
I got a self tape.

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:01.400
Really, what's interesting,
is in the final audition,

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.868
they brought us into this room,

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:05.133
and I seen how the camera was
just on a tripod right there.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:06.934
And I know I had to do something
different, right?

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.767
And in the first episode, if you
guys have seen it, my character

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.868
is looking into the camera like,
"What's up, guys?"

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:13.634
So I took the camera,
I picked it up

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:15.234
and I pointed it to myself.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.601
I'm like, "Yo, what's up?
These are my 'Rez Dog' friends."

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:20.100
And I showed
Taika and all of them.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.634
They really got it
involved with my scene.

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:24.267
I think that's a big reason why
I got it.

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.334
-How did you get the guts to do
that in an audition?

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:27.701
-I don't know.
I had to do something different.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.367
I had to do something different.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:32.033
-And, Paulina, you wanted to be
an action star.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:33.400
-Yes.
-Is that true?

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.601
-Yes, that's true.

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:36.834
-And I know that you are really
into sports.

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:39.667
Did you coach hockey
or you do coach hockey?

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:44.367
-Yes, I coached at a native
tournament called

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.400
Alberta Native Hockey
Provincials,

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.000
and I got to coach
the Alexis novice team.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.133
And that was pretty fun.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:54.968
Back home in my reserve,
we don't have a lot of

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:58.467
female hockey role models, so,
like, I get to be

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:01.701
a nice hockey role model
for my nieces and my nephews.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.300
-Yeah, you didn't have that
as a kid?

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.400
-No, I didn't have that
growing up.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.534
-Lane, you're still in school.

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:09.367
What do the other kids think
about all this?

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:11.601
You get treated differently?
Do you get special treatment?

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.334
-For the most part,
a lot of them don't know

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:14.667
or just don't care.
-Wow.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.534
[ Laughter ]
That's kids for you. Yeah.

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:20.267
-I have a few friends
who they ask,

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:21.667
"What are you going to do
when you go back to school?"

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.167
And, like, "What are you going
to do about them?"

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:26.767
I'm just like, well, not really
telling many people about it.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:29.067
A lot of people don't even know.
And some people who do know,

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:31.000
I just kind of stay quiet
about it.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.300
-Yeah. Do people go, like,

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.000
"Well, you're acting
like your character?"

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.300
Because you kind of act like
your character.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.100
-Yeah, I am -- I'm actually
pretty similar

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.801
to my character in,
like, many ways.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.067
-He is, right?
-Not very different from him.

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:45.400
-Are all you guys kind of
similar to -- do you -- like,

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.634
you're very -- you've got
good, funny one-liners

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.200
you throw out there.
-That's what I love about

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.334
the show 'cause, like, we're all
basically playing themselves.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.434
Like, they wanted rez kids,
they got rez kids.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.667
So, yeah.
-That's exactly right.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:59.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:02.000
You did.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.701
The show, can you set up
the show?

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.534
I don't know who is
the best to set it up

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:07.634
and tell everyone
what it's about.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.200
If you haven't seen it,
it's on Hulu.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.234
-"Reservation Dogs" is about
four native kids growing up

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:15.267
in a reservation and after they
lose their best friend,

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:17.400
they want to leave
the reservation.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.100
But as the show goes on,

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.434
they learn just how
really special it is

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.868
and they come to love it
and not wanting to leave at all.

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:26.868
-Yeah. That's good. That's
a good way to describe it.

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:31.100
It's very funny.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.634
It's very action-packed.

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:37.300
It's also very loving as well.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.801
And I think it's getting great
attention for this great acting

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.067
and directing
and all that stuff.

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:45.501
But also it's a culture that
I don't know much about.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.901
So I like seeing it and going,
"Oh, yeah"

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:50.133
and just going, "Oh, I want to
learn more about it."

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:51.334
Are there parts of the show that

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.567
you like better
than the other parts?

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:55.300
Do you like doing
the heist stuff?

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.133
Do you like doing the getting
in trouble stuff?

00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:59.434
Do you like being funny?
Do you like the dramatic acting?

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:03.033
-I love all the funny stuff.
-Native people are so funny.

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.501
And like, it's the first time
it's ever been shown before.

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:07.334
-Yeah.
-So that's why I think a lot of

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:09.634
people are falling in love with
it, because it's our humor.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:12.968
We're really funny people. It
just hasn't been shown before.

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:15.934
-Yeah. Good. I agree with you.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:19.033
Here's a sneak peek of season
two of "Reservation Dogs."

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:20.133
Take a look.

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:27.033
-I'll have sacred duties.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.501
-Who is he talking to?

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.067
-I think it's safe to say
he's delusional.

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:32.367
-Got to set a good example.
Help others.

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.901
-Uncle!
-What?

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:36.934
-The director's cut of
"Big Trouble in Little Ch--"

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.334
I've never seen this one.

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:41.100
-What the...are you kids
doing here?

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.934
-We need help.
-No.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.501
You caught me right
in the middle of

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:47.734
making myself a better man.

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:50.234
-What's that mean?
-It means get the...out.

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:52.534
Okay? What the...are you
doing with that?

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:56.567
-It was in the trash.
-My mistake.

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.634
Leave me alone.
-Yeah.

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:01.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
You have great chemistry.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:04.367
You guys are so good.
The cast of "Reservation Dogs."

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:07.467
Season two premieres
this Wednesday on Hulu.

